* Lab 22-10, Part 1 -- Example 22-10.6: a die's 20 uF of capacitance (with 0.1 mohm ESR) behind 2 pH of package
* inductance, fed from a stiff 0.8 V source, sees a 100 A load step with a 10 ps edge at t = 1 ns.
* (a) AC: the impedance seen from the die peaks near f0 = 1/(2 pi sqrt(LC)). (b) Transient: the first droop.
* EXPECT droop key:../../chapters/22-10-datacenter-power-delivery.md#Ex_22-10.6g scale=1e-3 rtol=1e-2
* EXPECT fpk key:../../chapters/22-10-datacenter-power-delivery.md#Ex_22-10.6a scale=1e6 rtol=1e-2
* EXPECT zpk key:README.md#Lab_22-10.a scale=1e-3 rtol=5e-3
.param L=2p C=20u RESR=0.1m
Vs src 0 dc 0.8
Lpkg src die {L}
Cdie die cx {C}
Resr cx 0 {RESR}
Iload die 0 dc 0 pwl(0 0 1n 0 1.01n 100) ac 1
.control
ac dec 400 1meg 1g
let zmag = mag(v(die))
meas ac zpk max zmag
meas ac fpk max_at zmag
tran 1p 60n 0 1p
meas tran vmin min v(die) from=1n to=30n
let droop = 0.8 - vmin
print droop
.endc
.end
